# Auto commit & push (Beta 1)

Until the user says otherwise (or after leaving Beta 1), **always commit and push** when finishing a task that changed the repo.

## When

- After implementing a fix, feature, or docs/Admin Manual update that should ship
- Do **not** wait for “commit and push” — treat that as already ordered

## How

Follow the repo’s normal git safety protocol:

- Commit only relevant files (no secrets, no unrelated untracked scripts unless part of the task)
- Use a concise why-focused message via HEREDOC
- Push to the current branch’s remote (`git push`)
- Never force-push `main`/`master`, never amend unless amend rules are met, never skip hooks

## Exceptions

- User explicitly says not to commit/push for that change
- Nothing to commit (empty / only ignored artifacts)
- Only exploratory/read-only work with no file changes

This project rule **overrides** the general “only commit when asked” preference for this repo during Beta 1.
